Interview Scenario Questions
Q1. Your Mule app needs to connect to a private Oracle DB in AWS. How will you do it?
Answer
"I would create a CloudHub VPC and establish VPC Peering with the customer's AWS VPC. After updating route tables and security groups, Mule can connect to the database using private IP addresses without exposing it to the internet."

Q2. Why use VPC Peering instead of public endpoints?
Answer
"VPC Peering improves security by keeping traffic on private networks, reduces exposure to the internet, lowers latency, and helps meet compliance requirements."

Q3. Is VPC Peering only for databases?
Answer
No.

It can connect to:

Databases
SAP
Internal REST APIs
Kafka
MQ Servers
Legacy applications
Q4. What networking information is needed for VPC Peering?
